          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01MdcFGvRqifuQizxDMWsDL3",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022pages/concepts/log-metric-correlation.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Log/Metric Correlation\\ndescription: Propagating trace context (trace_id, span_id) into logs and metric exemplars to enable operator pivoting from metric anomalies to their causal traces.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/Observability\\n  - concept/OpenTelemetry\\n  - pattern/Correlation\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Single authoritative source (OpenTelemetry definition); no corroboration yet.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\nLog/metric correlation is an observability pattern in which trace context \\u2014 specifically\\n\\u0060trace_id\\u0060 and \\u0060span_id\\u0060 \\u2014 is injected into both log records and metric exemplars. This\\nenables an operator to pivot seamlessly from a detected metric anomaly (e.g. a spike in\\nlatency or error rate) to the specific distributed traces that caused it.\\n\\n## Mechanism\\n\\nWhen a service emits a metric or writes a log entry, it attaches the active trace\\u0027s\\nidentifiers:\\n\\n- **Logs receive \\u0060trace_id\\u0060 and \\u0060span_id\\u0060**: Each timestamped structured log event\\n  carries the trace and span context of the request it belongs to.\\n- **Metrics receive exemplars**: An exemplar is a sample metric point enriched with\\n  trace context, allowing the metric to link to a specific trace that exemplifies\\n  the measured value at that moment.\\n\\n## Operational Value\\n\\nThis correlation allows an operator to:\\n\\n1. **Detect the anomaly** via a metric dashboard (e.g., \\u0022latency p99 spiked\\u0022).\\n2. **Retrieve causal traces** by following the exemplar or trace_id links from the\\n   metric or log.\\n3. **Debug root cause** by reading the full trace waterfall and associated logs.\\n\\nWithout correlation, a metric spike is an isolated signal; with correlation, it becomes\\na breadcrumb trail back to the specific request that triggered it.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: OpenTelemetry signal specification on traces, metrics, and correlation mechanics.\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
      "assistant_text": "## Analysis\n\nThe operator\u0027s task instruction is clear: **focus on log/metric correlation mechanics only** \u2014 skip the general three-signal-types overview (which they note is already covered elsewhere).\n\nThe source discusses:\n1. Three signal types (traces, metrics, logs) \u2014 operator says skip this, already covered\n2. **Log/metric correlation mechanics** \u2014 the focus: propagating trace_id/span_id into logs and exemplars on metrics\n\nThere is no existing page on OpenTelemetry, observability signal correlation, or logging/metrics correlation. I should create a focused page on **log/metric correlation mechanics**, following the operator\u0027s steering away from the general overview.\n\nThe source is minimal and authoritative (it defines OpenTelemetry concepts), so confidence will be \u0060medium\u0060 (single source, no corroboration yet).\n\nLet me create the focused page:",
